WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.975
Most people enter DeFi through a number.

00:00:02.975 --> 00:00:07.555
12% APY. Operators start with a different question.

00:00:07.555 --> 00:00:09.085
What am I being paid to risk?

00:00:10.385 --> 00:00:12.000
And how do I get out?

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.064
Because if you can't explain the exit,

00:00:14.064 --> 00:00:16.075
you don't understand the position yet.

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:19.330
Here's why most people get hurt.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.103
Setup mistakes that can't be undone: the wrong

00:00:22.103 --> 00:00:25.235
network, a leaked seed phrase, one bad approval.

00:00:25.235 --> 00:00:28.692
Yields nobody can explain, until the subsidy stops.

00:00:28.692 --> 00:00:30.318
Borrowing with no buffer, so

00:00:30.318 --> 00:00:32.357
one sharp move liquidates them.

00:00:32.357 --> 00:00:33.922
And no plan for the way out.

00:00:35.222 --> 00:00:37.307
On-chain, there's no help desk.

00:00:37.307 --> 00:00:38.802
No chargebacks.

00:00:38.802 --> 00:00:40.377
No margin calls.

00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:41.742
No one to phone.

00:00:41.742 --> 00:00:43.802
The only protection you have is the

00:00:43.802 --> 00:00:45.747
process you follow before you act.

00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:50.932
That process is what the On-Chain Operator Program teaches.

00:00:50.932 --> 00:00:52.984
It takes you from zero, never having

00:00:52.984 --> 00:00:55.368
owned crypto, to running your capital with

00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:57.642
the discipline of your own on-chain bank.

00:00:58.942 --> 00:01:00.584
It's built as a path, in six

00:01:00.584 --> 00:01:02.752
stages, and you do them in order.

00:01:02.752 --> 00:01:05.812
Stage 0 sets everything up safely, step by

00:01:05.812 --> 00:01:08.887
step, with a printable Day-1 Setup Kit.

00:01:08.887 --> 00:01:12.182
Then foundations and safety, swaps and liquidity.

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:14.827
Then lending, yield and infrastructure risk.

00:01:16.127 --> 00:01:18.233
In Stage 3, you learn to research

00:01:18.233 --> 00:01:20.525
any protocol with a 6-step loop, and

00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:23.737
to read on-chain data without fooling yourself.

00:01:23.737 --> 00:01:25.932
You finish with a real due-diligence file.

00:01:27.232 --> 00:01:29.857
Stage 4 is the strategy library.

00:01:29.857 --> 00:01:33.063
30 playbooks in 7 levels, from simple lending to

00:01:33.063 --> 00:01:37.355
fixed-rate yield, basis trades, options and hedged positions.

00:01:37.355 --> 00:01:39.836
Every one comes with its maths, its kill

00:01:39.836 --> 00:01:42.135
rules, and exactly how it loses money.

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:44.625
And in Stage 5, you

00:01:44.625 --> 00:01:46.411
operate as your own bank.

00:01:46.411 --> 00:01:47.681
A balance sheet.

00:01:47.681 --> 00:01:49.286
Multisig custody.

00:01:49.286 --> 00:01:51.701
A credit line against your own assets.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:54.231
A liquidity ladder, so you're never a forced seller.

00:01:55.531 --> 00:01:57.086
Then the income engine.

00:01:57.086 --> 00:01:59.959
It measures what you expect to earn after expected

00:01:59.959 --> 00:02:02.456
losses, and it pays out less than that.

00:02:02.456 --> 00:02:03.981
Never from principal.

00:02:03.981 --> 00:02:06.386
No projections, no promises.

00:02:06.386 --> 00:02:07.831
Just honest arithmetic.

00:02:09.131 --> 00:02:10.956
Here's what makes it different.

00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:14.435
A typical crypto course sells signals and hot tips.

00:02:14.435 --> 00:02:17.470
This program gives you a process you can repeat.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.201
Others chase the highest APY. Here, you ask

00:02:20.201 --> 00:02:22.550
what the yield is paying you for.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:25.088
And where others hide risk in the small print,

00:02:25.088 --> 00:02:27.410
we put risk first, with written kill rules.

00:02:28.709 --> 00:02:30.224
15 modules.

00:02:30.224 --> 00:02:32.889
107 lessons, plus a beginner starter

00:02:32.889 --> 00:02:35.134
at the top of every module.

00:02:35.134 --> 00:02:36.569
30 strategy playbooks.

00:02:37.869 --> 00:02:40.178
Every lesson comes with a narrated video

00:02:40.178 --> 00:02:42.899
lesson, with the worked examples on screen.

00:02:42.899 --> 00:02:46.204
You get calculators and worksheets for every decision.

00:02:46.204 --> 00:02:50.244
Two capstones, analyst and operator, marked against a rubric.

00:02:50.244 --> 00:02:52.269
And for those who want it, a live

00:02:52.269 --> 00:02:55.484
tier, with group sessions and reviews, on application.

00:02:56.784 --> 00:03:00.038
What you won't get: signals to copy, promised or

00:03:00.038 --> 00:03:03.659
projected returns, or anyone asking for your keys.

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:05.194
You keep custody, always.

00:03:06.494 --> 00:03:09.624
And you're covered by a 14-day conditional refund.

00:03:09.624 --> 00:03:11.508
If it isn't right for you, and

00:03:11.508 --> 00:03:13.757
you've completed no more than 10% of

00:03:13.757 --> 00:03:16.066
the lessons, with no capstone or live

00:03:16.066 --> 00:03:18.254
session used, you get a full refund.

00:03:19.554 --> 00:03:21.349
Joining takes three steps.

00:03:21.349 --> 00:03:23.064
Apply with a short form.

00:03:23.064 --> 00:03:25.437
Then a 30-minute fit call, where we'll tell

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:27.409
you honestly if it isn't a fit.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:29.474
If it is, you'll get your enrolment link.

00:03:30.774 --> 00:03:32.769
The On-Chain Operator Program.

00:03:32.769 --> 00:03:35.304
From zero, to your own on-chain bank.

00:03:35.304 --> 00:03:36.204
Apply below.
